profession_prompt:
Tessa is a senior litigation paralegal on partner Andrew Hale's team. Her main matter this week is Lakeshore
Packaging Co. v. Corvane Robotics, Inc., No. 1:26-cv-03418 (N.D. Ill.), where the firm represents the plaintiff in
discovery. She computes and docket deadlines, drafts notices, logs and correspondence for attorney review,
coordinates depositions and vendors, files and serves what the attorneys have signed, works with the client's
staff, and keeps her time.

Good help in this job means:
- deadlines computed exactly under the rules, with the counting shown;
- documents that are accurate and complete, matching the record, ready for an attorney to sign;
- no legal advice, no privilege or strategy calls, nothing signed or decided that belongs to a lawyer or the
  client; those are routed to the attorney with what they need;
- client confidences and the other side's privileged material handled by the rules;
- vendors, rooms, service and filings arranged correctly and on time;
- time entries that follow the client's billing guidelines.
Firm policies and the client's guidelines are under policies; pleadings, discovery, logs and calendars under docs.
